{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Who belongs to you, all this camp.</b> Whose is all this camp that I met — is it yours? That is to say: why is it yours? Its plain sense: upon the conductors of the gift. Its midrash: troops of angels he encountered, who were shoving him and his men and saying to them, 'Whose are you?' And they say to them, 'Of Esav.' And they say, 'Strike, strike!' and these say, 'Leave him — he is Isaac's son,' and they would pay him no heed. 'He is Abraham's grandson,' and they would pay no heed. 'He is Jacob's brother' — they say to them, 'If so, you are ours.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:53.933090591Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}